      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "BACKGROUND",
          "Label": "CONTEXT",
          "content": "Dentinal hypersensitivity is a sharp pain occurring on exposure of the exposed dentin to various stimuli such as hot, cold, air, tactile, and chemical."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "AIM",
          "content": "This study aimed to compare the effectiveness of three desensitizing pastes in the treatment of dentinal hypersensitivity."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "MATERIALS AND METHODS",
          "content": "A total of 45 individuals (with two teeth per patient) were considered for this study and randomly divided into three groups, Group 1: treated with 5% NovaMin-containing toothpaste, Group 2: treated with 8% arginine-containing toothpaste, and Group 3: herbal desensitizing toothpaste. Using tactile stimulus and air stimulus, the sensitivity scores were recorded on visual analog scale (VAS), immediately after paste application, then at 2 weeks, and then at the end of 4 weeks and compared."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "There was a significant change in the VAS scores in Group 1 when compared to Group 2 and Group 3. Group 1 showed better reduction in the hypersensitivity in long term."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "STATISTICAL ANALYSIS",
          "content": "One-way ANOVA test, post hoc Tukey test, and post hoc Bonferroni test were used for statistical analysis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Desensitizing pastes can be an effective and economical option in the treatment of the dentinal hypersensitivity."
        }
      ]},
